  "summary": "The study compares three Ti3C2Tx flexible PET-supported electrodes: pristine MXene, PVDF-MXene containing PVDF at a 1:10 PVDF:MXene mass ratio, and AFAO-MXene with an AFAO:MXene mass ratio of 1:10. All used Ti3C2Tx made by LiF/HCl etching, delamination, and DMSO processing; the AFAO sample additionally underwent alkoxysilane surface modification. The headline AFAO-MXene electrode achieved the highest reported capacitance, 219.1 F g\u22121 at 5 mV s\u22121 in 1 M H2SO4; its GCD capacitance was 208.3 F g\u22121 at 1 A g\u22121, while the conclusion instead reports 211.2 F g\u22121 at that current density. Electrode thickness, flake lateral size, BET surface area, porosity, pore diameter, tortuosity, and volumetric/areal capacitance were not reported."
}